{"name":"Bruise","hex":"#7e4071","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bruise","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To strike (a person), originally with something flat or heavy, but now specifically in such a way as to discolour the skin without breaking it; to contuse.","To damage the skin of (fruit or vegetables), in an analogous way."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A purplish mark on the skin due to leakage of blood from capillaries under the surface that have been damaged by a blow.","A dark mark on fruit or vegetables caused by a blow to the surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bruise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bruise","blocks":[{"text":"A bruise, also known as a contusion, is a type of hematoma of tissue, the most common cause being capillaries damaged by trauma, causing localized bleeding that extravasates into the surrounding interstitial tissues. Most bruises occur close enough to the epidermis such that the bleeding causes a visible discoloration. The bruise then remains visible until the blood is either absorbed by tissues or cleared by immune system action. Bruises which do not blanch under pressure can involve capillaries at the level of skin, subcutaneous tissue, muscle, or bone."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Pferdekuss.jpg/330px-Pferdekuss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bruise","wikidata":"Q574491"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Bl%C3%A5m%C3%A4rken.jpg/500px-Bl%C3%A5m%C3%A4rken.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Bl%C3%A5m%C3%A4rken.jpg/500px-Bl%C3%A5m%C3%A4rken.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A woman's bruising after a severe fall","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABl%C3%A5m%C3%A4rken.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Severebruise.jpg/500px-Severebruise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Severebruise.jpg/1280px-Severebruise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Severebruise.jpg/500px-Severebruise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bruise caused by colliding with a handrail, typical of extreme sports such as skateboarding and rollerblading.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeverebruise.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Sprained_foot.jpg/500px-Sprained_foot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Sprained_foot.jpg/1280px-Sprained_foot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Sprained_foot.jpg/500px-Sprained_foot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bruise caused by a sprained ankle","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASprained_foot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ca/Blaues_und_rotes_Auge_nach_Fu%C3%9Ftritt_ins_Gesicht_%28Ausschnitt%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ca/Blaues_und_rotes_Auge_nach_Fu%C3%9Ftritt_ins_Gesicht_%28Ausschnitt%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Black eye and subconjunctival hemorrhage after a punch to the face","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlaues_und_rotes_Auge_nach_Fu%C3%9Ftritt_ins_Gesicht_(Ausschnitt).jpg"},{"s